\uwave default
\noun default
\color inherit
 Since the regressors are strictly exogenous, then we can perform FGLS estimatio
n.
 To implement an FGLS procedure, we must assume the usual rank condition
 for GLS: 
\begin_inset Formula $\mbox{rank}E(Z_{i}^{\prime}\Omega^{-1}Z_{i})=(K+4)$
\end_inset

.
 So, 
\begin_inset Formula $\Upsilon$
\end_inset

 is now identified, and in a panel data context, the FGLS estimator that
 uses the variance matrix (44) is what is known as the random effects estimator
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{\beta}_{RE}=\left({\displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^{N}}Z_{i}^{\prime}\hat{\Omega}Z_{i}\right)^{-1}\left({\displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^{N}}Z_{i}^{\prime}\hat{\Omega}^{-1}y_{i}\right)
\]

\end_inset

where
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\hat{\Omega}\equiv\hat{\sigma}_{u}^{2}I_{T}+\hat{\sigma}_{a}^{2}j_{T}j_{T}^{\prime}
\end{equation}

\end_inset

In order to implement the RE procedure, we need to obtain 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{\sigma}_{a}^{2}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{\sigma}_{u}^{2}$
\end_inset

.
 First, we find 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{\sigma}_{v}^{2}=\hat{\sigma}_{a}^{2}+\hat{\sigma}_{u}^{2}$
\end_inset

.
 A consistent estimator of 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma_{v}^{2}$
\end_inset

 is
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{\sigma}_{v}^{2}=\frac{1}{(NT-K)}{\displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^{N}}{\displaystyle \sum_{t=1}^{T}}\check{v}_{it}^{2}
\]

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\check{v}_{it}=y_{it}-Z_{it}^{\prime}\Upsilon$
\end_inset

 denotes the pooled OLS residuals.
 Next, under our given assumptions, a 
\begin_inset Formula $\sqrt{N}$
\end_inset

- consistent estimator of 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma_{a}^{2}$
\end_inset

 is given by
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{\sigma}_{a}^{2}=\frac{1}{\left[\nicefrac{NT(T-1)}{2-K}\right]}{\displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^{N}}{\displaystyle \sum_{t=1}^{T-1}}\sum_{s=t+1}^{T}\check{v}_{it}\check{v}_{is}
\]

\end_inset

Given 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{\sigma}_{v}^{2}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{\sigma}_{a}^{2}$
\end_inset

, we can find 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{\sigma}_{u}^{2}=\hat{\sigma}_{v}^{2}-\hat{\sigma}_{a}^{2}$
\end_inset

 .
 Finally, under our given assumptions, the RE estimator is asymptotically
 equivalent to GLS, so it is the efficient in the class of estimators consistent
 under 
\begin_inset Formula $E(v_{i}|Z_{i})=0$
\end_inset

, including pooled OLS and a variety of weighted least squares estimators.
\end_layout

